WEBVTT

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:07.860
This story is one that lightly describes the ordinary daily lives of the three Minami sisters.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:10.440
Please don't expect too much from it.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.400
Also, watch in a bright room,

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.120
and stay 3 meters away from the TV while watching.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:23.370
Kana

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:23.710
Chiaki

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:24.620
Haruka

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:08.480
Another beautiful morning.

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:10.610
Oh no!

00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:51.190
Good morning, Haruka-neesama.

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:52.770
Good morning, Chiaki.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:58.740
Need help with anything?

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:00.360
Right...

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:02.950
Well then, peel the carrots for me.

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:03.950
Okay.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:08.750
Good morning!

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:11.960
Today is Sunday.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:14.790
The one day of the week with the most freedom.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:17.300
To confirm that freedom...

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:18.550
First...

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:20.170
Second nap!

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:22.050
Second nap, second nap, second nap.

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:23.220
Second nap, second nap!
Good night.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:24.220
Second nap, second nap!

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:27.560
That's it?

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.100
Can't you act a bit more concerned?

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.400
Like "even though your hair is already tied up"?

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.690
Or "help me with something!"

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:37.480
Well then, you can peel the potatoes.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:38.900
Roger!

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:44.240
Go to sleep already.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.240
That's so mean!

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:50.120
Three Minami Sisters

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:55.670
I'm home.

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:00.380
Welcome back.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:02.300
More like...

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:06.140
you should come home early and play with me.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:11.020
Treating me nicely, respecting me, and making me happy,

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:14.650
that's how you should act as my little sister!

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:16.610
Even so...

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:20.070
Where have you been all this time, you fool?

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:28.490
You give me this lame rhetoric, and yet you call me a fool?

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:30.370
You're hopeless already.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:33.120
I'm going to do my homework.

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:35.960
Sorry! Please play with me!

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:37.670
I have nothing to do!

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:40.800
Nothing to do, you say...

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.220
You're supposed to prepare dinner, right?

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:43.760
Eh?

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.720
I'm going to be late today,

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:48.550
so please take care of dinner.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:52.060
So that's what Haruka-neesama said, right?

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:53.060
Laters.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.360
Help me, Chiaki-sama.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.440
I have to finish my homework.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:04.650
You know about my cooking skills, right?

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:09.370
Do you know what would happen if you abandoned me now?

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:13.540
After you finish your homework and start feeling hungry,

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:16.120
you will be attacked by an unprecedented dish.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:18.330
There's more if you want.

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:21.880
I'll have you eat all of it...

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:27.300
So help me.

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:31.470
All right! So, what should we make?

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:35.060
We should check to see what's in the refrigerator first.

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:36.060
Okay!

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.520
Surprisingly, there's nothing left.

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:43.480
The chef is in a bad mood!

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:45.950
I can't cook with these ingredients!

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:49.200
What a cook needs are skills.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:52.030
Passion and good ingredients come next.

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:55.960
However, never mind skills, you don't even have passion.

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:58.290
If we can't even overcome those with ingredients,

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:01.920
we'll end up with rubbish produced from lumps of ego.

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:03.000
Where are you going?

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:06.470
I'm calling for delivery.

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:12.470
I'll make dinner.

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:14.560
I will not accept any third party interventions!

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:16.680
Kana, don't be angry.

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:20.400
A single phone call will return smiles to the dining table.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.980
If I back off here, I will lose my place as an elder sister!

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:26.690
Regarding that, it's too late to worry about that now.

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:30.160
I was just thinking that we've been too confined to the image of a typical dinner.

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:32.990
To forego common sense,

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:35.450
and try something simple and certainly delicious...

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:39.870
In other words, we should make pancakes!

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:42.420
Good.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:44.460
That's a great idea.

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:46.380
You did it, Kana!

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:47.920
Isn't that right?

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:49.970
You like pancakes, right?

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:53.010
Even an idiot can make that reasonably well.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:55.640
I shall toast you to a golden brown.

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:01.310
Hey, Chiaki.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:03.520
Let's put in fruit!

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:06.650
Yogurt also sounds good.

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:08.820
Let's put in juice too!

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:09.820
Wait a minute!

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:12.530
Amateur-like ignorance is a dangerous thing to have!

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:15.370
This is the most complete form for a pancake!

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:16.830
It's okay, it's okay.

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:18.790
They're all sweet foods; it'll fit.

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:20.000
All right!

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:23.710
One more!

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:27.250
Now, let's fry it!

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:32.300
I-It won't harden.

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:33.760
I-It won't harden.

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.100
Of course.

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:36.680
The material is thin.

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:37.930
Flour?

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:38.930
All gone.

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:44.440
Oh well...

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:47.110
Let's call it cream stew.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:50.570
I'm home.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:00.040
Sorry for being late.

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:05.080
Here, have some cream stew.

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:09.300
Look, there's more cream stew if you want.

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:11.840
I'm sorry.

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:14.590
Minami-ke.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:16.800
I hate you, Sensei!

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:18.220
Wait, Ninomiya-kun!

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:20.430
Let me go. Let me go, Sensei!

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:24.020
I've lied to you, the world...

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.600
I don't care about it anymore.

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:28.190
I love you, Ninomiya-kun.

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:30.360
Sensei...

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:38.700
<b>Loincloth Festival
As usual! Loincloth Festival Begins</b>

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:41.290
The usual loincloth festival has begun.
<b>Loincloth Festival
As usual! Loincloth Festival Begins</b>

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:44.250
Lots of visitors have come this year too.
<b>Loincloth Festival
As usual! Loincloth Festival Begins</b>

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:46.540
In other news...

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:48.040
Haruka-neesama.

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:51.210
A male teacher was kissing a female student just now...

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:53.800
Chiaki.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.380
Did you have fun at school?

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:58.100
Uh, yes.

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:07.230
Didn't you overreact just now?

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:08.690
Well...

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:12.740
I want Chiaki to have the proper knowledge, but...

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:17.200
I didn't know how to explain it so suddenly.

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:20.700
All right!

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:22.910
Then, as an elder sister,

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:25.460
I will teach her what kissing is.

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:27.750
Don't teach her anything strange.

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:34.590
Kana.

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:37.760
The male teacher was kissing a female student earlier...

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:38.800
That's right.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:40.680
Ah, about that...

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:44.890
Doesn't broadcasting that in prime time make the living room feel bad?

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:50.480
Right, it doesn't seem like something for the family to watch together.

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:52.360
A reasonable opinion

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:56.900
Well then, Chiaki.

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:59.410
Can you explain why it feels bad?

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:01.620
Explain, you say...

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:03.830
Because they shouldn't kiss, right?

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:07.870
What part of kissing is so wrong to you, then?!

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:09.670
Why are you so angry?

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:13.050
For someone who has never kissed, you should not deny kissing!

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:15.630
Have you done it?

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:18.130
Never.

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:26.140
Shall we try?

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:26.850
N-No.

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:27.600
N-No.

00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:09.890
Ouch...

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:12.400
Why you...

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:14.360
I said I didn't want to!
Why you...

00:11:14.360 --> 00:11:16.110
Aren't we sisters?

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:18.360
There's nothing to be embarrassed about!

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:19.650
Shut up!

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:23.280
Don't you know there are things that you can and can't do as sisters?

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:24.990
You fool!

00:11:33.790 --> 00:11:35.380
Wait!

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:48.600
Stop it!

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:52.850
What are you doing?

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:54.020
Kana, let go!
What are you doing?

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:58.360
Trying to kiss a truly unwilling sister.

00:11:58.360 --> 00:11:58.860
H-Haruka-neesama!

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:00.440
H-Haruka-neesama!

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:03.280
Stop it if she doesn't want to do it.

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:09.410
If it's Haruka, then you can kiss, right?

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:16.380
That's right.

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:18.630
Haruka is probably already experienced.

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:20.260
She should be able to teach you properly.

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:23.680
Now, the two of you together...

00:12:58.920 --> 00:12:59.420
Hey.

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:00.800
Kana, wake up.

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:06.090
You'll be late if you don't wake up.

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:13.850
It's an order from Haruka-neesama.

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:14.390
Wa-ke up.

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:14.850
Wa-ke up.

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:15.850
Wa-ke up.

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:35.120
Kana, are you awake?

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:39.000
What are you doing?

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:56.060
Where's the hostess and the chef?

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:58.020
Hey, fool.

00:13:58.020 --> 00:13:59.520
Hostess?

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:01.360
Who are you calling the hostess?

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:04.610
We've been saying all along that you'll be late. Don't you understand?

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:07.400
I understand what you're saying.

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:11.080
But isn't it bad for the body if we don't eat breakfast?

00:14:11.080 --> 00:14:14.040
Then, Haruka-neesama and I are just fine.

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:17.500
So as long as you two are okay, you're fine with everything?

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:20.960
The part about you being not okay doesn't bother me at all.

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:23.630
What a little sister...

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:25.550
But Haruka is different, right?

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:31.550
With this, you can eat on the way to school.

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:32.760
It's not enough.

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:35.720
Then, let's get up early tomorrow.

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:37.480
Not enough love.

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:42.020
You're really thoughtless.

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:43.070
What did you say?

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:45.480
Even if you make a fuss now,

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:48.320
you will only be late, and not make anyone happy.

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:50.530
But if you go to school...

00:14:50.910 --> 00:14:51.990
If I go...?

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:53.950
What will happen if I go?

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:57.750
Are you saying that my heart and body will be filled?

00:14:57.750 --> 00:14:58.710
Of course.

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:03.880
At school, there's this guaranteed source of food called school lunch, right?

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:11.590
Well then, comrades!

00:15:11.590 --> 00:15:13.550
We'll be late if we don't hurry up!

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:16.060
Let's go!

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:19.600
All rise!

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:21.060
Bow.

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:31.240
What's wrong, Kana?

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:33.410
You don't seem very energetic this morning.

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:34.410
It's unusual.

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:36.200
Keiko.

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:40.870
I... have never felt more like a fool than today.

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:45.420
To think that I was stirred by Chiaki this much.

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:46.090
D-Did something happen?

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:47.340
D-Did something happen?

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:51.930
School lunch... doesn't come out until lunch, right?

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:54.640
What about it?

00:15:56.850 --> 00:16:00.600
I wasn't expecting such a normal reaction.

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:01.940
Understand, Keiko.

00:16:01.940 --> 00:16:05.810
Right before your eyes, your best friend is collapsing due to an empty stomach!

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:07.940
Don't you want to save her?!

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:11.320
What should I do?

00:16:12.110 --> 00:16:14.070
Bring the school lunch to this place now.

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:16.070
Even if you tell me that,

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:19.040
we've only finished the first class.

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:22.710
Minions of Chiaki.

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:27.170
What are you saying I should do?

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:30.630
In the first place, Chiaki-chan has nothing to do with me...

00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:33.760
Ah, I'm so hungry.

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:53.860
Next Day

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:08.250
It's terrible!

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:20.310
It's terrible!

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:21.520
Move aside.

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:25.480
What's wrong, "boy who cried wolf"?

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:27.810
It's really terrible!

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:31.530
This was in my locker.

00:17:31.530 --> 00:17:33.900
Is this... a "love" letter?

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:37.780
Don't emphasize the "love" in "love letter"!

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:39.950
Was it already like this when you got it?

00:17:39.950 --> 00:17:44.370
No, that's because I crushed it when I held it too tightly in my sweaty hands.

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:48.420
So now you're at that age where you start receiving love letters too.

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:52.460
Haruka-neesama, age doesn't really have anything to do with it.

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:54.590
Can we read it?

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:55.130
D-Don't read it aloud.

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:57.260
D-Don't read it aloud.

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:04.390
"Sorry for sending you a letter so suddenly.

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:06.100
Ever since I met you,

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:10.230
I noticed I've always been following you with my eyes.

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:13.480
The lively and energetic you is on my mind.

00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:14.860
If it's okay with you,

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:19.280
I want to talk to you when no one is around in the classroom."

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:24.160
What an embarrassing guy.

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:26.290
Did you read it aloud?

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:29.210
Did you deliver your full emotions to our viewers?

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:32.290
It's a "love" letter from Fujioka-kun.

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:34.170
Stop that "love" thing.

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:36.630
What kind of person is Fujioka-kun?

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:39.890
Someone in the same class.

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:42.550
I'm pretty sure he is a regular on the soccer team,

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:46.480
and I heard he's very popular with girls...

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:50.440
Is that right?

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:53.610
If I bring him around, I would be able to brag about it.

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:57.110
Flaunting a brand name accessory around seems to suit you well.

00:18:57.110 --> 00:18:59.200
Are you envious, Chiaki?

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:00.070
Huh?

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:02.700
You're envious, aren't you?

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:04.490
Having this popular elder sister!

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:07.410
One who can walk around with a popular guy, this sister!

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:08.250
Get off.

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:09.460
Get down.

00:19:17.710 --> 00:19:19.470
It's okay to get excited,

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:21.970
but there are too many suspicious points with this letter.

00:19:22.970 --> 00:19:23.930
What is?

00:19:23.930 --> 00:19:26.600
For a man who has all his freedom with women,

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:30.140
why would he need to go through the trouble of sending a love letter to you?

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:31.350
I object!

00:19:31.350 --> 00:19:32.480
Overruled

00:19:33.020 --> 00:19:37.400
What bothers me is this part about the "lively and energetic you."

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:40.110
That's totally Kana, right?

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:42.280
Right, that's my only good point.

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:45.280
It's nothing to be proud of.

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:46.490
That's right.

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:48.250
That might be the reason.

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:49.410
What?

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:55.130
This part, you can read it as "you stand out too much."

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:58.760
And here, "when no one is around in the classroom,"

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:01.840
probably means "the fighting ring where no one can interfere."

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:04.550
A fighting ring where no one can interfere!

00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:10.140
When we decode all of the hidden messages...

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:12.270
The letter, in other words, becomes this:

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:14.350
Letter of challenge.

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:16.900
Haven't you been standing out too much recently?

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:18.480
You're an eyesore.

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:22.200
When there's no one around to interfere, let's talk with our fists.

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:24.740
The boss of ball-kicking, Fujioka.

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:26.870
So he's just a guy who's clumsy with words?

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:28.080
Unforgivable!

00:20:28.080 --> 00:20:31.460
Trying to crush my little maiden heart!

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:33.370
Calm down, Kana.

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:35.630
Your opponent is a specialist in leg techniques.

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:37.210
You can't win with a frontal attack.

00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:39.880
T-Then, what should I do, Chiaki-sama?

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:41.210
"Sama"?

00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:42.670
Fear not, big sister.

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:45.510
Let me teach you a special attack.

00:20:57.690 --> 00:20:58.980
Mi-Minami!

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:00.400
Mi-Minami!

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:14.160
Y-You know...

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:15.750
Y-You know...

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:16.750
I-I...

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:17.880
I-I...

00:21:26.590 --> 00:21:27.220
W-Why?

00:21:27.220 --> 00:21:28.470
W-Why?

00:21:28.470 --> 00:21:30.930
Your supporting leg is dead.

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:34.560
Therefore, your golden right is as good as dead.

00:21:34.560 --> 00:21:38.770
For having toyed with me, you should regret it.

00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:40.230
Eh?

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:50.410
I'm home!

00:21:51.740 --> 00:21:53.160
Welcome back.

